# FortressOS SMP Design

Status: DRAFT — all six pieces below are planning, not implementation. Follow
this sequence; each piece is a hard prerequisite for the next, and none
should begin until the previous piece is merged and actually verified (not
just planned) — mirrors the 9G scope-discipline precedent in ROADMAP.md.

Sequencing (fixed until discussed):

1. AP discovery & boot trampoline
2. Per-CPU storage (GS-base struct: current thread, lock tracker, syscall scratch, TSS)
3. Lock discipline under real concurrency
4. Scheduler: global runqueue + scheduler lock first; per-CPU runqueues later if needed
5. IPIs and TLB shootdown
6. Re-audit of the two-stage PMM/VMM init under concurrent AP bring-up

New binding invariants use ID prefix `SM`, following the existing L/S/I/M
convention in AGENTS.md §4. Evidence tables are left empty until real
verification exists — not filled in from the plan alone.

